  {
    "slug": "ba1-studies",
    "title": "BA1 Studies",
    "description": [
      "A collection of explorations from my first year, each telling a different story through fabric and form.",
      "These studies represent my early investigations into identity, memory, and social consciousness through fashion design.",
      "From tartan rebellion to delicate remembrance, each piece explores how clothing can carry meaning beyond its material form."
    ],
    "credits": "",
    "details": [],
    "date": "2023",
    "year": "BA1",
    "video": "/videos/BA1/studiesFilm.webm",
    "studies": [
      {
        "title": "Study of the Dress",
        "description": "Tartan, rebellion, and the raw beauty of imperfection. Inspired by Vivienne Westwood and the Scottish punk movement, where identity was loud and proud. It's about pride, rebellion, and the freedom to take up space. The shape is exaggerated, the stance strong. A tribute to individuality, to dressing as an act of resistance and pride.",
