      {
        "title": "Recycled Denim",
        "description": "This work started from my thoughts about homelessness, about what it means to have, or not have, a place to feel safe. To build something protective out of what is usually thrown away: recycled denim, plastic and an old sleeping bag. Each material holds traces of use, of care, of survival. It's about warmth, dignity, and the quiet wish for a softer world.",
