      {
        "title": "Paper Study",
        "description": "Inspired by Día de los Muertos, where life and death meet in color. Not as an ending, but as a continuation of life. The flowers, bright and fragile, became a symbol of memory and rebirth. It's a reflection on remembrance and renewal. Through layers of soft, pleated paper, I explored how something delicate can still carry meaning, how remembering can be both light and heavy at once. The layers echo the softness of flowers — fragile, temporary, yet full of life. Paper becomes a skin for memory, light enough to breathe, strong enough to hold what has passed.",
